    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Inserts missing days, weeks, months or other periods in each time series and fills values with zero, the previous value or interpolation, with a gap report.",
    "category": "Preparation",
    "subcategory": "Date",
    "tags": [
        "time series",
        "gaps",
        "fill",
        "calendar",
        "zero fill",
        "interpolate",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Transaction extracts only contain the days something happened: a product with no sales on Tuesday simply has no Tuesday row. Averages, charts and forecasts then silently skip the zero days.\n\nTime Series Filler inserts the **missing periods** in each series (per product, store, sensor...) so every series has one row per hour, day, week, month, quarter or year, then fills the value fields:\n\n- **Zero**: no row means nothing happened (sales, transactions, incidents)\n- **Previous value**: the last known value carries forward (prices, balances, stock levels)\n- **Linear interpolation**: straight line between known values (readings, temperatures)\n- **Leave empty**: insert the rows, keep the values missing\n\nEach series runs from its own first to last period, from the overall first to last period (so all series line up), or over a custom range. Inserted rows are flagged (*Is Inserted* = 1) and other fields can be carried forward. The second output reports, per series, expected and present periods, how many were inserted and the longest gap.\n\nWeeks run Monday to Sunday.",
